---The `Account` message represents a business's account within Merchant Center. It's the primary entity for managing product data, settings, and interactions with Google's services and external providers. Accounts can operate as standalone entities or be part of a advanced account structure. In an advanced account setup the parent account manages multiple sub-accounts. Establishing an account involves configuring attributes like the account name, time zone, and language preferences. The `Account` message is the parent entity for many other resources, for example, `AccountRelationship`, `Homepage`, `BusinessInfo` and so on. For more information, see [Sign up for Merchant Center](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/188924), [Manage accounts and settings](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/accounts/overview), [Create accounts](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/accounts/create-accounts), [Create test accounts](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/accounts/test-accounts), and [Filter accounts you can access](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/accounts/filter).
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Account
---@field timeZone? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TimeZone Required. The time zone of the account. On writes, `time_zone` sets both the `reporting_time_zone` and the `display_time_zone`. For reads, `time_zone` always returns the `display_time_zone`. If `display_time_zone` doesn't exist for your account, `time_zone` is empty. The `version` field is not supported, won't be set in responses and will be silently ignored if specified in requests.
---@field accountId? string Output only. The ID of the account.
---@field accountName? string Required. A human-readable name of the account. Don't use punctuation, capitalization, or non-alphanumeric symbols such as the "/" or "_" symbols. See [Adding a business name](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/12159159) for more information.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the account. Format: `accounts/{account}`
---@field adultContent? boolean Optional. Whether this account contains adult content.
---@field testAccount? boolean Output only. Whether this is a test account.
---@field languageCode? string Required. The account's [BCP-47 language code](https://tools.ietf.org/html/bcp47), such as `en-US` or `sr-Latn`.
---@field homePageUri? string Output only. URI (typically a URL) of the store's homepage.

