---Defines participation in a given program for the specified account. Programs provide a mechanism for adding functionality to a Merchant Center accounts. A typical example of this is the [Free product listings](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/13889434) program, which enables products from a business's store to be shown across Google for free. For more information, see [Manage programs](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/programs/overview). The following list is the available set of program resource IDs accessible through the API: * [`checkout`](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/products/checkout-settings) * `free-listings` * [`loyalty`](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/loyalty/loyalty-programs) * `product-ratings` * `shopping-ads` * [`ucp-integration` (limited access)](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/reference/rest/accounts_v1alpha/accounts.programs.ucpSettings) * [`youtube-affiliate`](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/14815513) * `youtube-shopping-checkout`
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Program
---@field unmetRequirements? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.RequirementList Output only. The requirements that the account has not yet satisfied that are affecting participation in the program.
---@field documentationUri? string Output only. The URL of a Merchant Center help page describing the program.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the program. Format: `accounts/{account}/programs/{program}`
---@field state? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.ProgramStateEnum Output only. The participation state of the account in the program.
---@field activeRegionCodes? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StringList Output only. The regions in which the account is actively participating in the program. Active regions are defined as those where all program requirements affecting the regions have been met. Region codes are defined by [CLDR](https://cldr.unicode.org/). This is either a country where the program applies specifically to that country or `001` when the program applies globally.

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.ProgramList gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Program[]

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.ProgramStateEnum "STATE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NOT_ELIGIBLE"|"ELIGIBLE"|"ENABLED"

