---The Merchant Center account's [shipping settings](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/6069284). The `ShippingSettings` resource lets you retrieve and update the shipping settings of your advanced account and all its associated sub-accounts. For more information, see [Manage shipping settings](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/accounts/manage-shipping-settings).
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.ShippingSettings
---@field etag? string Required. This field helps avoid async issues. It ensures that the shipping setting data doesn't change between the `get` call and the `insert` call. The user should follow these steps: 1. Set the etag field as an empty string for the initial shipping setting creation. 2. After the initial creation, call the `get` method to obtain an etag and the current shipping setting data before calling `insert`. 3. Modify the shipping setting information. 4. Call the `insert` method with the shipping setting information and the etag obtained in step 2. 5. If the shipping setting data changes between step 2 and step 4, the insert request will fail because the etag changes every time the shipping setting data changes. In this case, the user should repeat steps 2-4 with the new etag.
---@field services? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.ServiceList Optional. The target account's list of services.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the shipping settings. Format: `accounts/{account}/shippingSettings`. For example, `accounts/123456/shippingSettings`.
---@field warehouses? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.WarehouseList Optional. A list of warehouses which can be referred to in `services`.

---An object representing a short code, which is a phone number that is typically much shorter than regular phone numbers and can be used to address messages in MMS and SMS systems, as well as for abbreviated dialing (For example "Text 611 to see how many minutes you have remaining on your plan."). Short codes are restricted to a region and are not internationally dialable, which means the same short code can exist in different regions, with different usage and pricing, even if those regions share the same country calling code (For example: US and CA).
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.ShortCode
---@field regionCode? string Required. The BCP-47 region code of the location where calls to this short code can be made, such as "US" and "BB". Reference(s): - http://www.unicode.org/reports/tr35/#unicode_region_subtag
---@field number? string Required. The short code digits, without a leading plus ('+') or country calling code. For example "611".

---A list of store code sets sharing the same minimum order value. At least two sets are required and the last one must be empty, which signifies 'MOV for all other stores'. Each store code can only appear once across all the sets. All prices within a service must have the same currency.
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StoreCodeSetWithMov
---@field storeCodes? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StringList Optional. A list of unique store codes or empty for the catch all.
---@field value? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Price The minimum order value for the given stores.

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StoreCodeSetWithMovList gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StoreCodeSetWithMov[]

---A list of stores your products are delivered from. This is only valid for the local delivery shipment type.
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StoreConfig
---@field serviceRadius? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Distance Maximum delivery radius. This is only required for the local delivery shipment type.
---@field storeServiceType? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StoreConfigStoreServiceTypeEnum|string Indicates whether all stores, or selected stores, listed by this business provide local delivery.
---@field storeCodes? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StringList Optional. A list of store codes that provide local delivery. If empty, then `all_stores` must be true.
---@field cutoffConfig? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.CutoffConfig Configs related to local delivery ends for the day.

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StoreConfigStoreServiceTypeEnum "STORE_SERVICE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"ALL_STORES"|"SELECTED_STORES"

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StringList string[]

---A table defining the rate group, when `single_value` is not expressive enough.
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Table
---@field columnHeaders? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Headers Headers of the table's columns. Optional: if not set then the table has only one dimension.
---@field name? string Name of the table. Required for subtables, ignored for the main table.
---@field rows? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.RowList Required. The list of rows that constitute the table. Must have the same length as `row_headers`.
---@field rowHeaders? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Headers Required. Headers of the table's rows.

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TableList gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Table[]

---The `TermsOfService` message represents a specific version of the terms of service that merchants must accept to access certain features or services. For more information, see [Terms of Service](https://support.google.com/merchants/answer/160173). This message is important for the onboarding process, ensuring that merchants agree to the necessary legal agreements for using the service. Merchants can retrieve the latest terms of service for a given `kind` and `region` through `RetrieveLatestTermsOfService`, and accept them as required through `AcceptTermsOfService`. For step-by-step instructions, see [Manage Terms of Service](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/accounts/manage-tos-agreements).
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TermsOfService
---@field kind? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TermsOfServiceKindEnum The Kind this terms of service version applies to.
---@field regionCode? string Region code as defined by [CLDR](https://cldr.unicode.org/). This is either a country where the ToS applies specifically to that country or `001` when the same `TermsOfService` can be signed in any country. However note that when signing a ToS that applies globally we still expect that a specific country is provided (this should be merchant business country or program country of participation).
---@field fileUri? string URI for terms of service file that needs to be displayed to signing users.
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the terms of service version. Format: `termsOfService/{version}`
---@field external? boolean Whether this terms of service version is external. External terms of service versions can only be agreed through external processes and not directly by the merchant through UI or API.

---This resource represents the agreement state for a given account and terms of service kind. The state is as follows: * If the business has accepted a terms of service, `accepted` will be populated, otherwise it will be empty * If the business must sign a terms of service, `required` will be populated, otherwise it will be empty. Note that both `required` and `accepted` can be present. In this case the `accepted` terms of services will have an expiration date set in the `valid_until` field. The `required` terms of services need to be accepted before `valid_until` in order for the account to continue having a valid agreement. When accepting new terms of services we expect third-party providers to display the text associated with the given terms of service agreement (the url to the file containing the text is added in the Required message below as `tos_file_uri`). The actual acceptance of the terms of service is done by calling accept on the `TermsOfService` resource. `valid_until` field. For more information, see [Manage Terms of Service](https://developers.google.com/merchant/api/guides/accounts/manage-tos-agreements).
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TermsOfServiceAgreementState
---@field accepted? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Accepted Optional. The accepted terms of service of this kind and for the associated region_code
---@field name? string Identifier. The resource name of the terms of service version. Format: `accounts/{account}/termsOfServiceAgreementState/{identifier}` The identifier format is: `{TermsOfServiceKind}-{country}` For example, an identifier could be: `MERCHANT_CENTER-EU` or `MERCHANT_CENTER-US`.
---@field termsOfServiceKind? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TermsOfServiceAgreementStateTermsOfServiceKindEnum Required. Terms of Service kind associated with the particular version.
---@field regionCode? string Required. Region code as defined by https://cldr.unicode.org/. This is the country the current state applies to.
---@field required? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.Required Optional. The required terms of service

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TermsOfServiceAgreementStateTermsOfServiceKindEnum "TERMS_OF_SERVICE_KIND_UNSPECIFIED"|"MERCHANT_CENTER"

---@alias gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TermsOfServiceKindEnum "TERMS_OF_SERVICE_KIND_UNSPECIFIED"|"MERCHANT_CENTER"

---Represents a time zone from the [IANA Time Zone Database](https://www.iana.org/time-zones).
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TimeZone
---@field version? string Optional. IANA Time Zone Database version number. For example "2019a".
---@field id? string IANA Time Zone Database time zone. For example "America/New_York".

---Transit time table, number of business days spent in transit based on row and column dimensions. Either `min_transit_days`, `max_transit_days` or `transit_time_table` can be set, but not both.
---@class gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TransitTable
---@field postalCodeGroupNames? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StringList Required. A list of region names Region.name . The last value can be `"all other locations"`. Example: `["zone 1", "zone 2", "all other locations"]`. The referred postal code groups must match the delivery country of the service.
---@field rows? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.TransitTimeRowList Required. If there's only one dimension set of `postal_code_group_names` or `transit_time_labels`, there are multiple rows each with one value for that dimension. If there are two dimensions, each row corresponds to a `postal_code_group_names`, and columns (values) to a `transit_time_labels`.
---@field transitTimeLabels? gcp.unstable.merchantapi_accounts_v1.StringList Required. A list of transit time labels. The last value can be `"all other labels"`. Example: `["food", "electronics", "all other labels"]`.

